@startuml
title Nested amortisation — one recursive step, and the single final check
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
  StartColor #7A5BB5
  EndColor #7A5BB5
}

|Verification circuit at step i|
start
:read the deferred state from step i-1\n(G_old, S_old, y_old, u_old) as public input;
:partially verify the proof pi_i\nall checks except G = <s, G>, in O(log d);
:apply the amortisation argument\nmerging the new G with the deferred state;
:output (G_new, S_new, y_new, u_new)\nas public output, same fixed size;

|Verification circuit at step i+1|
:take that output as its public input;
:same structure, on the partner curve\nso that all arithmetic stays native;

|Ultimate verifier, outside every circuit|
:receive the final deferred state;
:perform the linear-time MSM once:\nG_final = <s_final, G>;
if (does it match?) then (yes)
  :accept the whole chain of T steps;
else (no)
  :reject;
endif
stop
@enduml
